public struct Image {
  public readonly width: u32;
  public readonly height: u32;
  public readonly pixels: Box<Slots<u8>>;
}

public enum PngError {
  Malformed();
  TooLarge();
}

public fn decode_png(data: &[u8]) -> result: Result<Image, PngError> reads(data) doc "Decodes the PNG datastream in data, under the PNG Specification, Third Edition, to non-premultiplied 8-bit RGBA: rows top to bottom, four bytes per pixel, so pixels holds width * height * 4 bytes. Every standard color type and bit depth and Adam7 interlacing are decoded. Palette entries and grayscale expand to RGB; grayscale below 8 bits scales by 255 / (2^depth - 1); a 16-bit sample keeps its most significant byte. Alpha comes from the image, or from tRNS: a palette entry's alpha, 255 past the end of the tRNS table, or 0 for a gray or RGB pixel equal to the tRNS key at the original bit depth; otherwise it is 255. Every other ancillary chunk is ignored, gamma and color space information and APNG frames past the static image included. TooLarge reports width * height above 2^26. Malformed reports every other failure: a wrong signature, a chunk CRC mismatch, an invalid IHDR, a missing or misplaced PLTE for a palette image, a palette index past the PLTE table, missing or nonconsecutive IDAT chunks, an unknown critical chunk, a zlib stream error or Adler-32 mismatch, too little image data, or a missing IEND.";
